.vercel

# Secrets: SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY bypasses row-level security entirely and
# GM_PASSWORD is the GM panel. See .env.example for the names without values.
.env*
!.env.example

# The generated roster: live two-word codes, and a code IS the player who holds
# it. The security model rests on codes never being fetchable — `players` has no
# anon SELECT policy for exactly that reason — so committing them would just
# move the credential behind a different lock, and git history is forever.
# Generated by scripts/, pasted into the SQL editor once; after that the
# database is the source of truth.
supabase/players.seed.sql
